OL,3,GNEWSAWorker at care home in BBC
OL,4,Ainvestigation given warning
OL,5,
OL,6,FA worker at a care home at the centre
OL,7,Fof a BBC investigation has been given a
OL,8,Fwarning after admitting causing
OL,9,Fdistress and agitation to a vulnerable
OL,10,Fresident.
OL,12,FA hearing was told Oluwabunmi Salami
OL,13,Fraised the bed of the resident without
OL,14,Fwarning, tried to take hold of his
OL,15,Fhands and failed to use any
OL,16,Fde-escalation techniques when he was
OL,17,Fshowing distress.
OL,19,FSalami has had conditions placed on her
OL,20,Flicence for three years, and been told
OL,21,Fto complete training within three
OL,22,Fmonths.
OL,23,APub: 17-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB  Scot NewsC Reg TVF  Weather
